        "title": "refactor(oc-path): privatize internal types",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe private `oc-path` implementation still exported 14 types and constants that\nhave no consumers outside their defining modules. Those unsupported exports also\nrequired permanent Knip baseline allowances, weakening the dead-code signal for\nthe package.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMake the zero-consumer declarations module-private and remove their matching\ndead-export baseline entries. The package entry point and all runtime functions\nremain unchanged; this deliberately excludes the JSONC parser surface touched by\n#104140.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior changes. Maintainers get a smaller internal export\nsurface and 14 fewer dead-code baseline exceptions.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Repository-wide exact-symbol search found each declaration only in its defining\n  module and internal type/function use.\n- Open PR overlap audit found only #104140, which touches the excluded JSONC parser\n  files and has no changed-file overlap.\n- Fresh Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxdhp9dcsd8w6b700rf6q9fb`, Actions run\n  `29244252603`:\n  - `pnpm deadcode:exports`: passed, 3280 entries.\n  - `pnpm test:extension oc-path`: 40/40 files and 706/706 tests passed.\n  - Targeted `pnpm check:changed`: formatting, production/test extension\n    typechecks, extension/script lint, package/storage/media/sidecar guards, and\n    runtime import-cycle checks passed.\n- Fresh `gpt-5.6-sol` medium autoreview: clean, 0.97 confidence.\n",
